    "body": "A Hazel program can now define a livelit and use it, live, below the definition:\n\n```\nlet ^pct = {\n  type Model = Int;\n  type Action = Int;\n  let init : Model = 50;\n  let update = fun (m, a) : (Model, Action) -> a;\n  let view = fun m : Model -> ...;   # HTML whose handlers emit Actions #\n  let expand = fun m : Model -> m\n} in\n^pct(25) + ^pct(75)\n```\n\nEach use elaborates to `^pct.expand(model)` through the runtime binding, so shadowing and scoping are ordinary let semantics, and each use's model lives in its own argument syntax \u2014 dragging a slider rewrites the number in the text and the result recomputes. The definition form is a module (equivalently a labeled or positional tuple); type members are accepted but not yet load-bearing; helpers and an optional `size = (w, h)` are ordinary members. Only `expand` runs during statics, built syntactically \u2014 no evaluation during elaboration. `update`/`view` run at render time via HazelDOM/MvuShape from the MVU work, so definitions must be closed.\n\nTwo doc slides ship as demos (\"Livelits / Define a Slider\", \"Livelits / Color Picker\" \u2014 an hwb picker with a clickable gradient square, which motivated a new `OnClickAt` attribute delivering element-relative click coordinates). Also fixes a pre-existing bug where every livelit projector in text-loaded slides rendered \"No livelit found\" (`get_model` didn't look through Projector/Parens wrappers).\n\n17 new tests (`UserLivelits`); suite at 3080 + doc-slide reparse green. Follow-up thinking on probe feedback inside definitions is recorded in `plans/livelit-probe-feedback.md`.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n---\n### Fix brought over from the aria-demo branch (2026-09-09)\n- fb9c1aab4e A livelit's model reaches the projector-side view evaluation as raw syntax with untyped constructors; ascribing such a constructor to its sum now types it instead of sticking (every `case` on the model in the view was stuck). Also merged hazel-html forward for its JSON ascription fix.\n",
